# The glass floor's chain (level.c's glass_anchor): every tile is sorted JO_3D_SORT_PREVIOUS behind
# one dot at the floor's deepest point. A tile jo cuts into parts near the camera moved the chain's
# key to its nearest corner, and the rest of the floor was then drawn over the grey boxes and the
# map (fixed in jo: the parts of a chained polygon keep the chain's key).
# Booted facing west at (9300, -250): a little way west, turned left (south), and walked slowly
# up to the grey box there (play-test 2026-11-08 at 8588, 162 facing south), a shot every step.
# Film it with tests\e2e\run_e2e.ps1 -Steps floor_chain.steps (built with BOOT_ON_FOOT 1)
wait_up # booted on foot in the corridor (BOOT_ON_FOOT): no ride there
hold up 0.9
wait 0.4
hold left 0.7
wait 0.4
shot fc_00_south
hold up 0.25
wait 0.3
shot fc_01
hold up 0.25
wait 0.3
shot fc_02
hold up 0.25
wait 0.3
shot fc_03
hold up 0.25
wait 0.3
shot fc_04
hold up 0.25
wait 0.3
shot fc_05
hold up 0.25
wait 0.3
shot fc_06
hold up 0.25
wait 0.3
shot fc_07
hold up 0.25
wait 0.3
shot fc_08
